<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PRODUCT_SPEC PLAY-002 — the car action while the book is *actually* coming out of the car.

  A device run asked for the one thing the Android Auto player does not show: *"the current audio output is
  not seen."* The host draws the title, the byline and these two icons, and nothing else this app supplies —
  so the icon is the only surface left to say it on. `ic_car_output` is the same glyph without the bar, and
  the pair reads as off/on side by side, which is how they are always drawn.

  The glyph is scaled to 0.84 rather than left at full size: at 24dp a bar tucked directly under an
  unscaled glyph touches it and the two read as one shape. The bar is 2.4 units of a 24-unit box, which is
  the smallest that survives the slot.
-->
